


   =====( SetCalls V1.00 )===========================================


        Trion SetCalls Utility.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   Setcalls is a little programm to set the amount of calls to
   your BBS. The amount of calls consist of Users and mailers
   who call your BBS.
   You can find the number of callers in the TrionRM monitor,
   and if you use tilde codes you can also display it in
   a screen on your BBS.

   When you setup the BBS for the first time you probably don't
   have to change the number of calls, but if you had an other
   BBS system running before Trion BBS you might want to set
   the number of calls.
   Or if you count the calls per year you might want to set the
   number of calls at the beginning of a year to zero.
   
   This utility was made to be integrated in an install script
   but nothing useable or practicall has materialized yet.

   When you want to use the setcalls Utility you have to make
   sure the BBS isn't running .. because if some one calls
   after you changed the number of calls when the system was
   online the file with the number of calls in it is overwritten
   with the old number. So TrionRM should not be running.

   You change the number of calls by typing setcalls in shell
   with the number of calls on the command line.
   The Utility will put the old number of calls on the screen.

